Size the video RTP receive buffer for the stream's bitrate. The fixed 2048 packets hold about
23 ms of video at 1 Gbps, so a short stall of the receive thread drops packets at the bitrates
Nightjar now allows (up to 2 Gbps). The buffer now holds about 60 ms at the configured bitrate
when that is more than the default; the OS still caps it at its own maximum.
Independent of the other patches; add it at the end of the list.

